<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vladislaus II of Bohemia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1110–1174</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Vladislav II of Bohemia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vladislaus II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> was Duke of Bohemia from 1140 and its second king from 1158, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> raised him to royal rank for supporting the emperor's Italian campaigns. Barbarossa also granted him the land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bautzen">Bautzen</a>, beginning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-lusatia">Upper Lusatia</a>'s long connection with the Bohemian crown.</p></div>
